== R5. O1: EOQ check rate equals 'nats per unit time' only formally ==
  EOQ: checks/time = 1/T*, mean error D_avg = sigma^2 T/2  =>  1/T = sigma^2/(2 D_avg). Thermo floor: nats/time = sigma^2/(2 D).
  So c/T == c * sigma^2/(2 D_avg): identifying one check with one nat makes the forms identical by construction.
  A perfect check acquires unbounded information (error -> 0), and info lost over a sawtooth cycle int_0^T dt/(2t) diverges:
    nats lost per cycle from error var eps*sigma^2*T to sigma^2*T: 2.30
    nats lost per cycle from error var eps*sigma^2*T to sigma^2*T: 4.61
    nats lost per cycle from error var eps*sigma^2*T to sigma^2*T: 6.91

